# Mantine-only frontend

All UI/UX in `frontend/` is built **only** from Mantine and its official ecosystem.

## Allowed

- `@mantine/core`, `@mantine/hooks`, `@mantine/form`, `@mantine/dropzone`, `@mantine/notifications`
- `@tabler/icons-react` (Mantine’s standard icons)
- `app/providers.tsx` — `MantineProvider` + `createTheme` only
- `frontend/lib/` — API client, types, constants (no UI)
- Mantine style props (`p`, `m`, `flex`, `gap`, `c`, `bg`, `h`, `mih`, etc.)

## Forbidden

- `frontend/components/` or any reusable UI component files
- Custom `.css` files (only `@mantine/*/styles.css` in root layout)
- Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, MUI, or any other UI library
- Inline `style={{ ... }}`
- Native HTML for UI (`<form>`, `<button>`, `<div>` layouts, `component="button"` on non-Mantine elements)
- `className` for custom styling

## Where to put UI

Compose screens in `frontend/app/` — `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` — using Mantine primitives directly.

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#frontend-ui).
